/**
 * Value handed down by `<Toolbar.Root>` to descendant parts.
 *
 * Solid 2 adaptations from Base UI React's `ToolbarRootContext`:
 *
 * - Reactive slots are `Accessor<T>` so children pull on demand without
 *   tripping the top-level-reactive-read rule.
 * - `present` is `true` only when provided by a real `<Toolbar.Root>`.
 *   Parts branch on it — `<Toolbar.Separator>` tolerates being rendered
 *   outside, and `<Toolbar.Button>` / `<Toolbar.Link>` throw (matching React).
